  "notes": "Clean security walk over 48 server-chunk files; no quantified, reproducible exploit introduced by the diff. Scope accounting (ACTION-REVIEW-SEC-004): (1) CROSS-CHUNK: bootstrapEnv (bootstrap.go:183) rejects only quotes and newlines in extra-prompt; $, backtick and backslash pass through as BOOTSTRAP_EXTRA_PROMPT. Safe only if cmd/bootstrap/run.sh consumes it as a quoted expansion and never via eval or an unquoted/bash -c string; verify in that chunk. (2) CROSS-CHUNK: POST /sessions/archive/{name}/delete passes PathValue (which decodes %2F, e.g. ..%2F..%2Fx) to sessions.DeleteScope; containment depends on internal/sessions name validation. (3) PRE-EXISTING, not introduced: sameOriginGuard (server.go:398, unchanged) never checks the Host header, so a DNS-rebinding page gets Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin. The new POST /welcome/bootstrap (attacker-chosen extra prompt into a multi-hour agent run) and POST /profile/style (text injected into every session's global context) widen that surface, but older routes (/api/config set hooks, /routines/{name}/run prompt) already allow equal or worse effects, and the listen address lives outside this chunk. (4) Not raised: bootstrap.go:71 opens a fixed os.TempDir()/smine-bootstrap.log with 0644 and follows symlinks. That only matters on a shared /tmp (Linux), while the supported platforms (launchd macOS, Windows logon task) use per-user temp dirs; the location itself is already in the known ledger as a spec issue.",
